me (17 items) 17 Staff Part-Time (1 items) 1 Staff Temporary (4 items) 4 Student (2 items) 2 Technical Instructor (4 items) 4 Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Accounts Specialist (Athletics) Topeka Accounting & Financial Services Accountants/Payroll/Purchasing Staff Full-time The Account Specialist supports Athletics and Finance Shared Services by providing accounting and administrative assistance to ensure financial tasks are completed accurately and on schedule. The role requires a strong customer service focus, effective communication and organizational skills, and the ability to use sound judgment in a variety of situations.\n\nThe position is responsible for a mix of technical and administrative accounting functions, including financial recordkeeping, transaction processing, and customer support. Duties include maintaining financial records, preparing and processing financial transactions, serving as the primary receptionist for Athletics, and assisting departments with financial procedures in compliance with established policies and guidelines. More complex matters are referred to appropriate personnel as needed.\n\nAs part of the Finance Shared Services team, this role provides accounting and reporting support across campus. Work assignments and work locations between Washburn University and Washburn Institute of Technology may vary according to operational needs; however, the primary office location will be Athletics. Read more Adjunct (Biology) Topeka College of Arts & Sciences Biology/Chemistry/Physics/Astronomy Adjunct Washburn University's Department of Biology invites applications for adjunct faculty position(s). Read more Adjunct (Chemistry) Topeka College of Arts & Sciences Biology/Chemistry/Physics/Astronomy Adjunct Washburn University's College of Arts and Sciences, Chemistry department, invites applications for the position of Adjunct instructor. Read more Adjunct (English) Topeka College of Arts & Sciences English, Modern Languages Adjunct Washburn University's department of English invites applications for adjunct faculty. Read more Adjunct (Medical/Surgical Clinicals) Topeka School of Nursing Nursing Adjunct Washburn University's Harmony J. Hines School of Nursing invites applications for adjunct faculty positions to teach medical/surgical clinicals, academic year 2026-2027. Registered nurses interested in working with students and have an active Kansas license are encouraged to apply. Placements are available in both acute and long-term care. Read more Adjunct (Modern Languages-Spanish) Topeka College of Arts & Sciences English, Modern Languages Adjunct Washburn University's Department of Modern Languages invites applications for academic year 2026-2027 adjunct faculty position(s). Read more Adjunct (School of Law) Topeka School of Law Law, Legal Studies, Forensics Adjunct Washburn University School of Law invites applications for an adjunct instructor to teach a variety of courses beginning in the 2026-2027 academic year. Read more Anthropology Special Project Lab Assistant Topeka Forensic Center Clinical Lab Assistants Staff Temporary Washburn University is accepting applications for an Anthropology Special Project Lab Assistant. Read more Assistant Chief Engineer (Updated 7/7/20026) Topeka KTWU Arts, Museum Admin, Television Staff Full-time Assistant Chief Engineer opportunity open with KTWU, PBS in Topeka, KS! KTWU, licensed by Washburn University, is looking for someone who understands the technology, equipment, and processes associated with the broadcast and digital platform distribution of content to Kansas communities. The Assistant Chief Engineer is a key component of the KTWU Engineering Team, who will work closely with the Chief Engineer to install, maintain, and repair KTWU's transmission equipment for broadcast in NE and SE Kansas and stay on top of technological trends and changes that impact equipment, operations, and viewership. We encourage anyone with experience in broadcast technology and an understanding of broadcast, digital, mobile, and online technologies to apply for this new position at KTWU. There will be opportunities for advancement within the KTWU Engineering Team. Read more Assistant Coach, Cross Country and Track – Recruiting Coordinator Topeka Men's Intercollegiate Athletics Athletics, Coaches Staff Full-time Washburn University is accepting applications for an Assistant Coach, Cross Country and Track – Recruiting Coordinator. Read more Assistant General Counsel Topeka President General Counsel/Legal Staff Staff Full-time Washburn University is accepting applications for an Assistant General Counsel. Read more Assistant Professor (Clinical, Counseling, or School Psychology) Topeka College of Arts & Sciences Psychology, Sociology, Anthropology, Philosophy Faculty Tenure Track Washburn University's Department of Psychology invites applications for an assistant professor position to begin January or August 2027.  This is a full-time 9-month, tenure track position. A completed doctorate is necessary for tenure-track appointment. Read more Associate Professor (Legal Analysis, Research, and Writing) Topeka School of Law Law, Legal Studies, Forensics Faculty Tenure Track Washburn University School of Law invites applicants for a tenured/tenure-track position to teach first year Legal Analysis, Research and Writing, beginning in the 2027-2028 academic year.  Washburn Law’s nationally ranked legal writing program follows the typical structure for legal writing courses: objective or predictive writing in the first semester and persuasive writing and advocacy in the second semester. Both courses are three credit hours. Washburn Law has a unitary tenure track with scholarship support including summer writing grants, year-round research assistants, and funding for travel to conferences. This nine-month tenured/tenure-track position is one of three open tenured/tenure-track positions in the School of Law. Read more Associate Professor (Small Business and Nonprofit Transactional Law Clinic) Topeka School of Law Law, Legal Studies, Forensics Faculty Tenure Track Washburn University School of Law invites applicants for a tenured/tenure-track position to teach in the Washburn Law Clinic and to teach complementary doctrinal courses, beginning in the 2027-2028 academic year. Washburn Law has a unitary tenure track with scholarship support including summer writing grants, year-round research assistants, and funding for travel to conferences. This nine-month tenured/tenure-track position is one of three open tenured/tenure-track positions in the School of Law. Read more Associate Professor or Professor (Doctrinal) Topeka School of Law Law, Legal Studies, Forensics Faculty Tenure Track WASHBURN UNIVERSITY SCHOOL OF LAW invites applicants for a tenured/tenure-track position, beginning in the 2027-2028 academic year. We are especially interested in candidates who would teach constitutional law, administrative law, legislation, property, evidence, professional responsibility, or remedies. Washburn Law has a unitary tenure track with scholarship support including summer writing grants, year-round research assistants, and funding for travel to conferences.  This nine-month tenured/tenure-track position is one of three open tenured/tenure-track positions in the School of Law. Read more Building and Grounds Technician (Two positions) Topeka WIT-Administration Custodians / Landscape Techs Staff Full-time Washburn University is accepting applications for two Building and Grounds Technicians. Read more Campus Safety Dispatcher (Part-time, Temporary) (Two Positions) Topeka University Police Police and Public Safety Staff Temporary Washburn University is accepting applications to hire two Campus Safety Dispatchers. Read more Carpenter Topeka Facilities Services Facilities Maint/HVAC/Mgmt. Staff Full-time Washburn University is accepting applications for a Carpenter. Read more Construction Project Manager (Updated 8/24/2026) Topeka Facilities Services Architecture/Planning/Engineering Staff Full-time Wonderful Benefits - Personal Leave, Sick Leave, Retirement Contributions, Health Insurance, Holidays, etc. Read more Cosmetology Substitute Instructor Topeka WIT-Other Technical Programs Vocational Career/Training/Advising Staff Part-Time Washburn University is accepting applications for a Cosmetology Substitute Instructor. The grand opening of our new center is scheduled for August 7th! Read more Director of Non-Discrimination Initiatives – Title IX Administrator Topeka President Human Resources/EEO/Title IX Staff Full-time This position oversees Washburn’s compliance efforts with Title IX, Title VI, Title VII, the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA), Section 504, NCAA membership compliance, and related Washburn policies and state and federal laws. Read more Executive Assistant Topeka President Admin Support, Exec Assistants Staff Full-time The EA is primarily responsible for providing administrative support to the Office of the President, as directed by the Senior Executive Assistant to the President, and to the Title IX, Equal Opportunity Director. Read more Facilities and Systems Technician II (Updated 7/7/20026) Topeka College of Arts & Sciences Arts, Museum Admin, Television Staff Full-time The Facilities and Systems Technician II (Technician) is responsible for the operation and maintenance of audio, video, and lighting systems required for live performances and events for the Department of Music and Theatre, and/or university events. Read more Graduate Assistant - Athletics External Relations Topeka Office of the Director of Athletics Student Employee Student This position offers a unique opportunity for the selected candidate to gain hands-on experience in the intercollegiate sports industry. The individual will play a key role in enhancing the Washburn Athletics brand, expanding its fanbase, and elevating the overall gameday experience within the highly competitive Mid-America Intercollegiate Athletics Association (MIAA), the premier conference in NCAA Division II. The selected candidate will assist with all aspects of Washburn Athletics External Relations. Read more Graduate Assistant - Ticketing and Sales Topeka Office of the Director of Athletics Student Employee Student This position offers a unique opportunity for a highly motivated and detail-oriented individual to gain hands-on experience in intercollegiate athletics. The selected candidate will play a vital role in supporting Washburn Athletics’ ticketing and sales efforts, enhancing customer service operations, and contributing to the development of corporate sponsorships. Reporting directly to the Director of Sales, the Graduate Assistant for Ticketing and Sales will assist with all aspects of ticket operations and revenue generation, helping to elevate the fan experience and drive engagement within the highly competitive Mid-America Intercollegiate Athletics Association (MIAA), the premier conference in NCAA Division II.\n\nThis position is ideal for a graduate student pursuing a career in sports management, sales, or athletic administration. Read more Instructional Librarian Topeka University Library Librarians Faculty Lecturer Washburn University's University Libraries invites applications for Instructional Librarian to begin October 1, 2026. This is a 12-month, benefit eligible, full-time position. \n\nThe Instructional Librarian provides general and virtual information, research, and reference services, plans, teaches and assesses information literacy instruction in collaboration with the Associate Dean of University Libraries and other appropriate staff. In addition, based upon disciplinary interest, expertise, and Unit needs, the Librarian will support other library initiatives, including but not limited to: faculty and student research, digital projects, First and Second-Year Student Success Initiatives, collection development, scholarly communication, Open Access and Open Educational Resources, Artificial Intelligence, outreach, and assessment. Read more Lecturer (Sociology) Topeka College of Arts & Sciences Psychology, Sociology, Anthropology, Philosophy Faculty Lecturer Washburn University's Department of Sociology and Anthropology invites applications for a Sociology Lecturer to begin in August 2027. This is a full-time, nine-month, non-tenure-track position with a renewable annual contract. Read more Maintenance Technician (Four Positions) (Updated 7/7/20026) Topeka Facilities Services Facilities Maint/HVAC/Mgmt. Staff Full-time This position performs the duties of a Maintenance Technician. Read more Medical Billing and Coding Custom Training Specialist Topeka WIT-Other Technical Programs Vocational Career/Training/Advising Staff Temporary Washburn Institute of Technology is accepting applications for a Medical Billing and Coding Custom Training Specialist.\n\nWashburn is dedicated to recruiting and retaining a dynamic faculty, staff, and student body and cultivating a robust learning and working environment and curriculum. We employ more than one thousand faculty and staff on our campuses throughout Topeka and strive to offer competitive wages, an excellent benefits program, and a supportive culture and a healthy work/life balance. Washburn seeks to create an environment that reflects our core values for creating positive IMPACT: inclusion, modernization, partnership, achievement, community and transformation. In 2024, Washburn was recognized as one of the best colleges in the nation to work for, according to Great Colleges to Work For® program. Read more Medication Aide Clinical Lab Assistant and/or Nurse Aide Clinical Lab Assistant Topeka WIT-Health Occupations Clinical Lab Assistants Staff Temporary Washburn University is accepting applications for a Medication Aide Clinical Lab Assistant and/or Nurse Aide Clinical Lab Assistant. Read more Displaying 1 - 30 of 40 in total ‹ 1 2 › 1700 SW COLLEGE AVE TOPEKA, KANSAS 66621 785.670.1010 Memorial Union Mulvane Art Museum Disability Services Statements & Disclosures My Washburn Jobs Calendar Site Map Washburn University prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, age, national origin, ancestry, disability, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, genetic information, veteran status, or marital or parental status. The following person has been designated to handle inquiries regarding the non-discrimination policies: Michelle White-Godinet, Title IX Equal Opportunity Director, Washburn University, 1700 SW College Ave, Topeka, Kansas 66621, 785.670.1509, eodirector@washburn.edu . Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations, analyze our traffic and support our marketing efforts. By clicking “I Accept” or using the website you agree to our use of cookies. Please read our Web Privacy Statement for more information. If you prefer not to receive cookies, you may turn them off in your browser, or may set your browser to ask you before accepting a new cookie. I do not accept I accept"
