ication, Open Access and Open Educational Resources, Artificial Intelligence, outreach, and assessment. Read more Lecturer (Sociology) Topeka College of Arts & Sciences Psychology, Sociology, Anthropology, Philosophy Faculty Lecturer Washburn University's Department of Sociology and Anthropology invites applications for a Sociology Lecturer to begin in August 2027. This is a full-time, nine-month, non-tenure-track position with a renewable annual contract. Read more Maintenance Technician (Four Positions) (Updated 7/7/20026) Topeka Facilities Services Facilities Maint/HVAC/Mgmt. Staff Full-time This position performs the duties of a Maintenance Technician. Read more Medical Billing and Coding Custom Training Specialist Topeka WIT-Other Technical Programs Vocational Career/Training/Advising Staff Temporary Washburn Institute of Technology is accepting applications for a Medical Billing and Coding Custom Training Specialist.\n\nWashburn is dedicated to recruiting and retaining a dynamic faculty, staff, and student body and cultivating a robust learning and working environment and curriculum. We employ more than one thousand faculty and staff on our campuses throughout Topeka and strive to offer competitive wages, an excellent benefits program, and a supportive culture and a healthy work/life balance. Washburn seeks to create an environment that reflects our core values for creating positive IMPACT: inclusion, modernization, partnership, achievement, community and transformation. In 2024, Washburn was recognized as one of the best colleges in the nation to work for, according to Great Colleges to Work For® program. Read more Medication Aide Clinical Lab Assistant and/or Nurse Aide Clinical Lab Assistant Topeka WIT-Health Occupations Clinical Lab Assistants Staff Temporary Washburn University is accepting applications for a Medication Aide Clinical Lab Assistant and/or Nurse Aide Clinical Lab Assistant. Read more Displaying 1 - 30 of 40 in total ‹ 1 2 › 1700 SW COLLEGE 