    "https://careers.washburn.edu/jobs/accounts-specialist-athletics-topeka-kansas-united-states": {
      "title": "Accounts Specialist (Athletics)",
      "description": "Accounts Specialist (Athletics) - Topeka, Kansas, United States Home About Us Academics Admissions Student Life Athletics See all jobs Applicant Settings Kiosk mode Accounts Specialist (Athletics) Accounting & Financial Services Apply Now Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Accounts Specialist (Athletics) Accounting & Financial Services Staff Full-time Add to favorites View favorites Position Title: Accounts Specialist (Athletics) Department: Finance Office Advertised Pay: $20.19/hour Campus Location: Washburn University Application Deadline: Application review will begin as applications are received and will continue until the position is filled. Position Summary: This position supports Athletics and Finance Shared Services by providing accounting and administrative assistance to ensure financial tasks are completed accurately and on schedule. The role requires a strong customer service focus, effective communication and organizational skills, and the ability to use sound judgment in a variety of situations. The position is responsible for a mix of technical and administrative accounting functions, including financial recordkeeping, transaction processing, and customer support. Duties include maintaining financial records, preparing and processing financial transactions, serving as the primary receptionist for Athletics, and assisting departments with financial procedures in compliance with established policies and guidelines. More complex matters are referred to appropriate personnel as needed. As part of the Finance Shared Services team, this role provides accounting and reporting support across campus. Work assignments and work locations between Washburn University and Washburn Institute of Technology may vary according to operational needs; however, the primary office location will be Athletics. About Washburn University: Washburn University is a teaching-focused, student-centered, public institution located in the metropolitan setting of Topeka that has earned national recognition for its high-impact programs for first-generation students. Washburn has a student body of just over 7,000 students, a significant and growing number of whom are first-generation and Pell-Grant eligible. The University has created educational pathways for all students to be successful and achieve their educational goals. Washburn is dedicated to recruiting and retaining a dynamic faculty, staff, and student body and cultivating a robust learning and working environment and curriculum. We employ more than one thousand faculty and staff on our campuses throughout Topeka and strive to offer competitive wages, an excellent benefits program, and a supportive culture and a healthy work/life balance. Washburn seeks to create an environment that reflects our core values for creating positive IMPACT: inclusion, modernization, partnership, achievement, community and transformation. In 2024, Washburn was recognized as one of the best colleges in the nation to work for, according to Great Colleges to Work For® program. Essential Functions: • Serve as the main point of contact for the Athletics department, welcoming visitors and managing incoming calls. • Interpret and apply Washburn accounting policies, procedures, and chart of accounts structure (FOAPAL). • Ensure compliance with federal, state, NCAA, and Washburn policies, procedures, and regulations. • Utilize accounting and office systems to complete assigned financial tasks efficiently and accurately. • Review financial transactions for accuracy, completeness, and proper coding; identify and resolve routine discrepancies. • Compile and prepare reports related to receipts, expenditures, and account activity. • Deliver responsive, professional, and courteous customer service to internal and external stakeholders. • Participate in cross-training to support continuity of Finance operations. • Maintain strict confidentiality of financial, employee, and student records. • Track orders and payments; verify receipt and accuracy of goods and services in coordination with departments prior to processing payments. • Prepare and process payment vouchers in accordance with Washburn procedures. • Create and submit University One Card expense reports. • Prepare travel requests and process travel expense reports. • Prepare and process deposits in accordance with established timelines and procedures. • Prepare routine journal entries and account adjustments. • Process transfer requests between funding sources. • Create and process purchase requisitions in compliance with procurement guidelines. • Provide administrative and operational support to Athletics and Finance Shared Services. • Assist Financial Reporting and Academic Budgets with preparation, documentation, and maintenance of reports and records. • Perform additional job-related duties as assigned. Non-Essential Functions: • Assist with special projects, process improvements, and documentation updates. • Support the development and maintenance of task manuals and procedures. • Participate in training and professional development opportunities to enhance skills and support departmental knowledge sharing. Required Qualifications: • High school diploma, GED, or equivalent. • Two years of accounting, bookkeeping, or related administrative experience. • Experience with a computerized accounting system. • Highly detail-oriented and organized, with effective time-management skills, and the ability to balance multiple priorities while meeting ongoing deadlines. • Effective written and verbal communication skills. • Proven proficiency in Microsoft Excel. Preferred Qualifications: • Experience with ERP systems such as Ellucian Banner. • Intermediate Excel skills, including pivot tables, advanced formulas, and data analysis/combination techniques. • Experience working in an Athletic Department. • Successful completion of two or more college-level accounting courses. Hourly, full-time, Mon-Fri, 8am-5pm Background Check Required Washburn University is committed to providing an environment for individuals to pursue educational and employment opportunities free from discrimination and/or harassment. The University prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, age, national origin, ancestry, disability, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, genetic information, veteran status, or marital or parental status. Washburn University is committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants for employment. If you are an applicant who needs a reasonable accommodation to participate in the application or interview process, please email benefits@washburn.edu or call 785-670-1538 at least five (5) business days in advance of the date you need the requested accommodation. Apply Now Want to hear about jobs like this one? First Name (required) 562aee39 Last Name (required) 624700fa Email (required) 2bb03edb Job Alert 540be4b7 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Accounting & Financial Services Accounting & Financial Services Categories Accountants/Payroll/Purchasing Accountants/Payroll/Purchasing Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Campus Safety Dispatcher (Part-time, Temporary) (Two Positions) University Police Washburn University is accepting applications to hire two Campus Safety Dispatchers. Technical Instructor (Associate Degree Nursing) WIT-Health Occupations Washburn University Institute of Technology seeks applications for a Technical Instructor for the Associate Degree Nursing program. There are currently two positions available for immediate hire. This is a 10-month, full-time position with benefits. This position is expected to work Monday-Friday 7:30 am – 4:00 pm. This position will also work varying clinical hours. Anthropology Special Project Lab Assistant Forensic Center Washburn University is accepting applications for an Anthropology Special Project Lab Assistant. Retail Specialist Memorial Union Washburn University is accepting applications for a Retail Specialist. Instructional Librarian University Library Washburn University's University Libraries invites applications for Instructional Librarian to begin October 1, 2026. This is a 12-month, benefit eligible, full-time position. \n\nThe Instructional Librarian provides general and virtual information, research, and reference services, plans, teaches and assesses information literacy instruction in collaboration with the Associate Dean of University Libraries and other appropriate staff. In addition, based upon disciplinary interest, expertise, and Unit needs, the Librarian will support other library initiatives, including but not limited to: faculty and student research, digital projects, First and Second-Year Student Success Initiatives, collection development, scholarly communication, Open Access and Open Educational Resources, Artificial Intelligence, outreach, and assessment. Upward Bound Advisor University Library Washburn University is accepting applications for an Upward Bound Advisor. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) f2a4fd01 Last Name (required) 09c5c92c Email (required) e9cfe7ae Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you 1700 SW COLLEGE AVE TOPEKA, KANSAS 66621 785.670.1010 Memorial Union Mulvane Art Museum Disability Services Statements & Disclosures My Washburn Jobs Calendar Site Map Washburn University prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, age, national origin, ancestry, disability, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, genetic information, veteran status, or marital or parental status. The following person has been designated to handle inquiries regarding the non-discrimination policies: Michelle White-Godinet, Title IX