    "https://careers.washburn.edu/jobs/adjunct-medical-surgical-clinicals-topeka-kansas-united-states": {
      "title": "Adjunct (Medical/Surgical Clinicals)",
      "description": "Adjunct (Medical/Surgical Clinicals) - Topeka, Kansas, United States Home About Us Academics Admissions Student Life Athletics See all jobs Applicant Settings Kiosk mode Adjunct (Medical/Surgical Clinicals) School of Nursing Apply Now Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Adjunct (Medical/Surgical Clinicals) School of Nursing Adjunct Add to favorites View favorites Position Title: Adjunct (Medical/Surgical Clinicals) Department: Nursing Campus Location: Washburn University Position Summary: Washburn University's Harmony J. Hines School of Nursing invites applications for adjunct faculty positions to teach medical/surgical clinicals, academic year 2026-2027. Registered nurses interested in working with students and have an active Kansas license are encouraged to apply. Placements are available in both acute and long-term care. Each selected candidate will have a demonstrated commitment to pursuing teaching excellence at Washburn University, including a dedication to developing inclusive teaching practices that engage all learners. About Washburn University: Washburn University is a teaching-focused, student-centered, public institution located in the metropolitan setting of Topeka that has earned national recognition for its high-impact programs for first-generation students. Washburn has a student body of just over 7,000 students, a significant and growing number of whom are first-generation and Pell-Grant eligible. The University has created educational pathways for all students to be successful and achieve their educational goals. Washburn is dedicated to recruiting and retaining a dynamic faculty, staff, and student body and cultivating a robust learning and working environment and curriculum. We employ more than one thousand faculty and staff on our campuses throughout Topeka and strive to offer competitive wages, an excellent benefits program, and a supportive culture and a healthy work/life balance. Washburn seeks to create an environment that reflects our core values for creating positive IMPACT: inclusion, modernization, partnership, achievement, community and transformation. In 2024, Washburn was recognized as one of the best colleges in the nation to work for, according to Great Colleges to Work For® program. Essential Functions: Availability or class schedule: • Options of one or two days per week are available. • Clinical rotations are 8 weeks in length. Responsibilities • Include working with a small group of students in the clinical setting assisting with providing patient care. • Facilitating communication with the agency staff. • Assisting students with communication to other healthcare providers, patients, and families. • Ensuring facility documentation is completed by the student. • Supervising medication administration and completion of skills. • Grading student work. • Assisting with on-campus skills checkoffs and simulation. Required Qualifications: • BSN • Minimum of two-year’s experience in the nursing field • RN licensed in Kansas • Demonstrated dedication to developing inclusive teaching practices that engage all learners. • RN licensed in Kansas • Official educational transcripts are required at the time of hire. Preferred Qualifications: MSN or working on MSN Special Instructions to Applicants: Questions pertaining to this position may be directed to Dr. Debbie Isaacson, debbie.isaacson@washburn.edu . Applications will be reviewed as received and based on department need. Background Check Required Washburn University is committed to providing an environment for individuals to pursue educational and employment opportunities free from discrimination and/or harassment. The University prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, age, national origin, ancestry, disability, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, genetic information, veteran status, or marital or parental status. Washburn University is committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants for employment. If you are an applicant who needs a reasonable accommodation to participate in the application or interview process, please email benefits@washburn.edu or call 785-670-1538 at least five (5) business days in advance of the date you need the requested accommodation. Apply Now Want to hear about jobs like this one? First Name (required) ddea1a4f Last Name (required) 5cdf3c15 Email (required) 34707a7f Job Alert a39daf7f Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments School of Nursing School of Nursing Categories Nursing Nursing Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Campus Safety Dispatcher (Part-time, Temporary) (Two Positions) University Police Washburn University is accepting applications to hire two Campus Safety Dispatchers. Technical Instructor (Associate Degree Nursing) WIT-Health Occupations Washburn University Institute of Technology seeks applications for a Technical Instructor for the Associate Degree Nursing program. There are currently two positions available for immediate hire. This is a 10-month, full-time position with benefits. This position is expected to work Monday-Friday 7:30 am – 4:00 pm. This position will also work varying clinical hours. Anthropology Special Project Lab Assistant Forensic Center Washburn University is accepting applications for an Anthropology Special Project Lab Assistant. Retail Specialist Memorial Union Washburn University is accepting applications for a Retail Specialist. Instructional Librarian University Library Washburn University's University Libraries invites applications for Instructional Librarian to begin October 1, 2026. This is a 12-month, benefit eligible, full-time position. \n\nThe Instructional Librarian provides general and virtual information, resea