    "https://careers.washburn.edu/jobs/assistant-coach-cross-country-and-track-recruiting-coordinator-topeka-kansas-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant Coach, Cross Country and Track – Recruiting Coordinator",
      "description": "Assistant Coach, Cross Country and Track – Recruiting Coordinator - Topeka, Kansas, United States Home About Us Academics Admissions Student Life Athletics See all jobs Applicant Settings Kiosk mode Assistant Coach, Cross Country and Track – Recruiting Coordinator Men's Intercollegiate Athletics Apply Now Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Assistant Coach, Cross Country and Track – Recruiting Coordinator Men's Intercollegiate Athletics Staff Full-time Add to favorites View favorites Position Title: Assistant Coach, Cross Country and Track – Recruiting Coordinator Department: XC Track and Field Men Advertised Pay: Lower $40,000's Campus Location: Washburn University Application Deadline: Application review will begin as applications are received and will continue until the position is filled. Applicants can be assured of full consideration if submitted by 5pm, August 21, 2026. Position Summary: This position is responsible for assisting the Head Coach in the general leadership of the men’s and women’s cross country/track and field teams. This position will have the primary role of recruiting coordinator, which includes scouting and recruiting quality student athletes to the program. The position is expected to conduct all assigned tasks in a manner that supports program compliance with NCAA, MIAA, and Washburn University policies, rules, and regulations. About Washburn University: Washburn University is a teaching-focused, student-centered, public institution located in the metropolitan setting of Topeka that has earned national recognition for its high-impact programs for first-generation students. Washburn has a student body of just over 7,000 students, a significant and growing number of whom are first-generation and Pell-Grant eligible. The University has created educational pathways for all students to be successful and achieve their educational goals. Washburn is dedicated to recruiting and retaining a dynamic faculty, staff, and student body and cultivating a robust learning and working environment and curriculum. We employ more than one thousand faculty and staff on our campuses throughout Topeka and strive to offer competitive wages, an excellent benefits program, and a supportive culture and a healthy work/life balance. Washburn seeks to create an environment that reflects our core values for creating positive IMPACT: inclusion, modernization, partnership, achievement, community and transformation. In 2024, Washburn was recognized as one of the best colleges in the nation to work for, according to Great Colleges to Work For® program. Essential Functions: • Assist with coaching and developing the skills of Washburn Track and Field athletes. • Provide individual and group coaching and guidance to assist with running practices, workouts, and meets. • Responsible for scouting, contacting, and tracking potential student athletes within the guidelines of the program’s model. • Responsible for organizing official and unofficial visits for potential student athletes invited to campus. • Assist the head coach with the operation of home meets; track the academic progress and success of recruits and current student athletes; and assist in the coordination of fundraising, camps, clinics, and special events. • Performs additional job-related duties as assigned or as appropriate. Required Qualifications: • Bachelor’s degree. • Experience coaching and/or participating in cross country and/or track. • Demonstrated effective interpersonal and organizational skills. • Ability to communicate effectively with student athletes, coaches, staff, and parents. • Valid driver's license with an acceptable driving record under Washburn's standards. Preferred Qualifications: • Master’s degree. • Collegiate participation in cross country and/or track. Exempt, Full-time Background check and driving history are required. Washburn University is committed to providing an environment for individuals to pursue educational and employment opportunities free from discrimination and/or harassment. The University prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, age, national origin, ancestry, disability, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, genetic information, veteran status, or marital or parental status. Washburn University is committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants for employment. If you are an applicant who needs a reasonable accommodation to participate in the application or interview process, please email benefits@washburn.edu or call 785-670-1538 at least five (5) business days in advance of the date you need the requested accommodation. Apply Now Want to hear about jobs like this one? First Name (required) 4525d706 Last Name (required) 29958a69 Email (required) d5866ee0 Job Alert 47e01fbb Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Men's Intercollegiate Athletics Men's Intercollegiate Athletics Categories Athletics, Coaches Athletics, Coaches Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Campus Safety Dispatcher (Part-time, Temporary) (Two Positions) University Police Washburn University is accepting applications to hire two Campus Safety Dispatchers. Technical Instructor (Associate Degree Nursing) WIT-Health Occupations Washburn University Institute of Technology seeks applications for a Technical Instructor for the Associate Degree Nursing program. There are currently two positions available for immediate hire. This is a 10-month, full-time position with benefits. This position is expected to work Monday-Friday 7:30 am – 4:00 pm. This position will also work varying clinical hours. Anthropology Special Project Lab Assistant Forensic Center Washburn University is accepting applications for an Anthropology Special Project Lab Assistant. Retail Specialist Memorial Union Washburn University is accepting applications for a Retail Specialist. Instructional Librarian University Library Washburn University's University Libraries invites applications for Instructional Librarian to begin October 1, 2026. This is a 12-month, benefit eligible, full-time position. \n\nThe Instructional Librarian provides general and virtual information, research, and reference services, plans, teaches and assesses information literacy instruction in collaboration with the Associate Dean of University Libraries and other appropriate staff. In addition, based upon disciplinary interest, expertise, and Unit needs, the Librarian will support other library initiatives, including but not limited to: faculty and student research, digital projects, First and Second-Year Student Success Initiatives, collection development, scholarly communication, Open Access and Open Educational Resources, Artificial Intelligence, outreach, and assessment. Upward Bound Advisor University Library Washburn University is accepting applications for an Upward Bound Advisor. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) 60d2a8b7 Last Name (required) 7b4059c0 Email (required) ac943aeb Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you 1700 SW COLLEGE AVE TOPEKA, KANSAS 66621 785.670.1010 Memorial Union Mulvane Art Museum Disability Services Statements & Disclosures My Washburn Jobs Calendar Site Map Washburn University prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, age, national origin, ancestry, disability, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, genetic information, veteran status, or marital or parental status. The following person has been designated to handle inquiries regarding the non-discrimination policies: Michelle White-Godinet, Title IX Equal Opportunity Director, Washburn University, 1700 SW College Ave, Topeka, Kansas 66621, 785.670.1509, eodirector@washburn.edu . Candidate Detail