    "https://careers.washburn.edu/jobs/carpenter-topeka-kansas-united-states-99578e79-9462-4a6f-b24a-5efa0e516f71": {
      "title": "Carpenter",
      "description": "Carpenter - Topeka, Kansas, United States Home About Us Academics Admissions Student Life Athletics See all jobs Applicant Settings Kiosk mode Carpenter Facilities Services Apply Now Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Carpenter Facilities Services Staff Full-time Add to favorites View favorites Position Title: Carpenter Department: Facilities Services (CBU) Advertised Pay: $21.63/hour Campus Location: Washburn University Application Review: Application review will begin as applications are received and will continue until the position is filled. Position Summary: This position performs the duties of a Carpenter. About Washburn University: Washburn University is a teaching-focused, student-centered, public institution located in the metropolitan setting of Topeka that has earned national recognition for its high-impact programs for first-generation students. Washburn has a student body of just over 7,000 students, a significant and growing number of whom are first-generation and Pell-Grant eligible. The University has created educational pathways for all students to be successful and achieve their educational goals. Washburn is dedicated to recruiting and retaining a dynamic faculty, staff, and student body and cultivating a robust learning and working environment and curriculum. We employ more than one thousand faculty and staff on our campuses throughout Topeka and strive to offer competitive wages, an excellent benefits program, and a supportive culture and a healthy work/life balance. Washburn seeks to create an environment that reflects our core values for creating positive IMPACT: inclusion, modernization, partnership, achievement, community and transformation. In 2024, Washburn was recognized as one of the best colleges in the nation to work for, according to Great Colleges to Work For® program. Essential Functions: • Employees are expected to use equipment to manufacturer and University standards and to comply with University and OSHA policies and regulations. • New employees must complete safety training within 6 months of hire. • As assigned or requested via work orders, construct, repair and maintain structures such as furniture, partitions, walls, platforms, paneling, siding, window frames, stairways, doors and door frames and other structures using hand and power tools and performing a variety of construction duties, including but not limited to carpentry, plastering, ceiling tile and grid repairs; roof repairs such as wooden trim, soffit or shingle roof tiles; floor repair such as install small quantity of floor tiles or patch floor tiles; and masonry and minor demolition. • Review building plans, blueprints, sketches, etc., estimate and requisition type and quantity of materials required to complete projects. • Work with other facilities and University staff, offices, etc. to coordinate activities to accomplish carpentry work. • Install and maintain doors. • Maintain and repair locks on doors, windows, and furniture. • Record and document completed tasks using Computerized Maintenance Management System software. • Inspect completed work for quality standards, code, and regulation compliance. • Recommend work process improvements to Facilities supervisors and administrators. • Assist with general maintenance activities as assigned. • Provide service support for campus events. • Maintain a professional, safe, and clean work area. • Snow removal duties as assigned. Required Qualifications: • High school diploma, GED, or equivalent. • A combination of five (5) years of experience working as a Carpenter acquired through on-the-job training and/or a completed certification program. • Ability to communicate effectively verbally and in writing. • Ability to read and apply information from schematics and building blueprints. • Valid driver's license with an acceptable driving record under Washburn's standards. Physical Requirements: • This position is designated a safety sensitive position and will be required to undergo drug screening. • Ability to work from a ladder and/or a lift. • Ability to respond to emergency service calls outside regularly scheduled work hours. • Ability to move and/or maneuver equipment and materials weighing as much as 50 pounds. Preferred Qualifications: • Skills as a locksmith. • Experience with a Computerized Maintenance Management System. Hourly, Full-time, Mon-Fri, 8am-4:30pm Background check, driving history, and drug screen are required. Washburn University is committed to providing an environment for individuals to pursue educational and employment opportunities free from discrimination and/or harassment. The University prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, age, national origin, ancestry, disability, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, genetic information, veteran status, or marital or parental status. Washburn University is committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants for employment. If you are an applicant who needs a reasonable accommodation to participate in the application or interview process, please email benefits@washburn.edu or call 785-670-1538 at least five (5) business days in advance of the date you need the requested accommodation. Apply Now Want to hear about jobs like this one? First Name (required) 5efe046a Last Name (required) d7180661 Email (required) fca8600f Job Alert 52c8dbb0 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Facilities Services Facilities Services Categories Facilities Maint/HVAC/Mgmt. Facilities Maint/HVAC/Mgmt. Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Campus Safety Dispatcher (Part-time, Temporary) (Two Positions) University Police Washburn University is accepting applications to hire two Campus Safety Dispatchers. Technical Instructor (Associate Degree Nursing) WIT-Health Occupations Washburn University Institute of Technology seeks applications for a Technical Instructor for the Associate Degree Nursing program. There are currently two positions available for immediate hire. This is a 10-month, full-time position with benefits. This position is expected to work Monday-Friday 7:30 am – 4:00 pm. This position will also work varying clinical hours. Anthropology Special Project Lab Assistant Forensic Center Washburn University is accepting applications for an Anthropology Special Project Lab Assistant. Retail Specialist Memorial Union Washburn University is accepting applications for a Retail Specialist. Instructional Librarian University Library Washburn University's University Libraries invites applications for Instructional Librarian to begin October 1, 2026. This is a 12-month, benefit eligible, full-time position. \n\nThe Instructional Librarian provides general and virtual information, research, and reference services, plans, teaches and assesses information literacy instruction in collaboration with the Associate Dean of University Libraries and other appropriate staff. In addition, based upon disciplinary interest, expertise, and Unit needs, the Librarian will support other library initiatives, including but not limited to: faculty and student research, digital projects, First and Second-Year Student Success Initiatives, collection development, scholarly communication, Open Access and Open Educational Resources, Artificial Intelligence, outreach, and assessment. Upward Bound Advisor University Library Washburn University is accepting applications for an Upward Bound Advisor. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) 9143a322 Last Name (required) 45e14d59 Email (required) 8d0f888c Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you 1700 SW COLLEGE AVE TOPEKA, KANSAS 66621 785.670.1010 Memorial Union Mulvane Art Museum Disability Services 