    "https://careers.washburn.edu/jobs/executive-assistant-topeka-kansas-united-states": {
      "title": "Executive Assistant",
      "description": "Executive Assistant - Topeka, Kansas, United States Home About Us Academics Admissions Student Life Athletics See all jobs Applicant Settings Kiosk mode Executive Assistant President Apply Now Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Executive Assistant President Staff Full-time Add to favorites View favorites Position Title: Executive Assistant Department: President's Office Advertised Pay: Base $24.68/hour with potential for a higher entry rate commensurate with experience Campus Location: Washburn University Application Review: Application review will begin as applications are received and will continue until the position is filled. Position Summary: The Executive Assistant (EA) for the President’s Office reports to and is supervised by the Senior Executive Assistant to the President. The EA will carry out responsibilities as outlined below. The normal work hours for the EA will be Monday through Friday from 8:00 a.m. to 5:00 p.m. The EA will need to have a flexible work schedule to staff special events, including but not limited to events at the President’s residence and commencement. These events may occur early in the morning, in the evening, or on the weekends. About Washburn University: Washburn University is a teaching-focused, student-centered, public institution located in the metropolitan setting of Topeka that has earned national recognition for its high-impact programs for first-generation students. Washburn has a student body of just over 7,000 students, a significant and growing number of whom are first-generation and Pell-Grant eligible. The University has created educational pathways for all students to be successful and achieve their educational goals. Washburn is dedicated to recruiting and retaining a dynamic faculty, staff, and student body and cultivating a robust learning and working environment and curriculum. We employ more than one thousand faculty and staff on our campuses throughout Topeka and strive to offer competitive wages, an excellent benefits program, and a supportive culture and a healthy work/life balance. Washburn seeks to create an environment that reflects our core values for creating positive IMPACT: inclusion, modernization, partnership, achievement, community and transformation. In 2024, Washburn was recognized as one of the best colleges in the nation to work for, according to Great Colleges to Work For® program. Essential Functions: Office Administrative Support The EA is primarily responsible for providing administrative support to the Office of the President, as directed by the Senior Executive Assistant to the President, and to the Title IX, Equal Opportunity Director. Primary responsibilities under the Office of the President include the following: • This role is an extension of the Office of the President and Board of Regents and must display the highest level of professionalism and confidentiality with the ability to demonstrate tact, calm, diplomacy, and problem-solving skills with a customer service mindset. • Contribute to a working environment that is team-oriented, anticipatory, supportive, and collaborative. • Demonstrate ability to establish and maintain cooperative relationships with those contacted in the course of work and respond to sensitive matters and/or situations with discretion, tact, and confidentiality. • Assist with the daily operations of the Office of the President and manage the President’s Residence (Ross House) in collaboration with the Senior Executive Assistant. • Responsible for the distribution of the President’s Honor Roll. • Serve as the backup to the Senior Executive Assistant (SEA) to the President and assist with the following functions as directed: o Schedule meetings as directed by the President or Chief of Staff. o Maintain the President’s day-to-day schedule. • Responsible for business expense-related tasks for the Office of the President, including processing permissible transactions using the Washburn issued credit card, ordering supplies, submitting internal requests, and similar tasks, following established Washburn policies and procedures. • Maintain high-profile decorum in the office in speech, demeanor, manners, and professional attire. • Provide event administrative support for special events from conception to clean-up for the President’s Office and the President’s residence: o Work with the Senior Executive Assistant to determine the budget for each event. o Attend events when required to direct final preparations, resolve problems that may arise, and ensure that the events run smoothly. o Assist with planning meetings to establish timelines and deadlines for all aspects of the events. o Plan and order catering as needed. o Manage invitation guest lists, mail or email invitations, and collect RSVPs. o Serve as liaison with vendors on event-related matters. o Process expenditures related to Presidential events. o Work collaboratively with other Washburn and Foundation staff when events are co-sponsored. • Attend all Washburn fall and spring commencement ceremonies, including the Washburn Tech and Washburn Law ceremonies, and help with the following: o Work within the commencement budget to order and purchase supplies and arrange services required for commencement. o Work with the Senior Executive Assistant to finalize all details related to the commencement ceremonies. o Work with Washburn departments such as the Ichabod Shop (to facilitate order and distribution of graduation regalia and apparel), academic units (to distribute name cards and honor cords for the ceremony), facilities services (to ensure appropriate and timely set-up of stage and chairs), external vendors (florist, printing, etc.), and others as necessary to facilitate their commencement preparations. o Compile information and collaborate to ensure the development of the commencement program and work with the printer to ensure timely delivery. o Process expenditure related to commencement activities. Primary responsibilities under the Title IX, Equal Opportunity Director include the following: • Manage the Title IX, Equal Opportunity Director’s calendar, coordinating with internal and external partners including but not limited to scheduling or rescheduling meetings/trainings, conference meetings, and on-site visits. • Order supplies for the Director in accordance with Washburn policies and procedures. • Responsible for all business expense-related tasks for the Title IX, Equal Opportunity Director, including processing permissible payment vouchers and transactions using the Washburn issued credit card following established Washburn policies and procedures. • Arrange travel (flights, hotels, car services, registration, etc.) as requested. Submit travel documentation (receipts, meeting itineraries) for processing for the Title IX, Equal Opportunity Director. • Assist in monitoring the Title IX, Equal Opportunity Director’s budget. • Maintain filing systems including confidential files for the Equal Opportunity Office. • Prepare professional and accurate correspondence as needed. • May field complaints brought to the Office of the President and the Title IX, Equal Opportunity Director. Answer questions and/or refer callers to appropriate individuals based on Washburn policies and procedures. • Contribute to the overall success of Washburn by performing additional job-related duties and responsibilities as assigned or as appropriate. Required Qualifications: • Bachelor's degree or a combination of post-secondary education and relevant administrative support experience equivalent to a degree, plus three years of relevant experience. • Demonstrated ability to successfully manage complex tasks while maintaining strong organization, effective time management, excellent customer service, and close attention to detail. • Ability to work independently and with a team construct. • Demonstrated effective interpersonal and verbal and written communication skills. • Demonstrated proficiency in typical office technology and software programs. (i.e. Excel, Word, PowerPoint, Outlook, Adobe, Zoom, Teams, etc.). • Ability to maintain confidentiality and work independently. • Demonstrated ability to prepare high-quality written materials, ensuring accuracy, consistency, and adherence to organizational standards. Preferred Qualifications: • A bachelor's degree. • Two or more years of relevant and progressively responsible administrative and project management work experience in a college or university, or a similarly complex public or private organization. • Experience supporting an executive-level office or legal office. • Experience organizing and managing events. Hourly, Full-Time Background Check Required Washburn University is committed to providing an environment for individuals to pursue educational and employment opportunities free from discrimination and/or harassment. The University prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, age, national origin, ancestry, disability, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, genetic information, veteran status, or marital or parental status. Washburn University is committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants for employment. If you are an applicant who needs a reasonable accommodation to participate in the application or interview process, please email benefits@washburn.edu or call 785-670-1538 at least five (5) business days in advance of the date you need the requested accommodation. Apply Now Want to hear about jobs like this one? First Name (required) 923cacb4 Last Name (required) ccc8bd34 Email (required) ae712fff Job Alert 26325ddd Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments President President Categories Admin Support, Exec Assistants Admin Support, Exec Assistants Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Campus Safety Dispatcher (Part-time, Temporary) (Two Positions) University Police Washburn University is accepting applications to hire two Campus Safety Dispatchers. Technical Instructor (Associate Degree Nursing) WIT-Health Occupations Washburn University Institute of Technology seeks applications for a Technical Instructor for the Associate Degree Nursing program. There are currently two positions available for immediate hire. This is a 10-month, full-time position with benefits. This position is expected to work Monday-Friday 7:30 am – 4:00 pm. This position will also work varying clinical hours. Anthropology Special Project Lab Assistant Forensic Center Washburn University is accepting applications for an Anthropology Special Project Lab Assistant. Retail Specialist Memorial Union Washburn University is accepting applications for a Retail Specialist. Instructional Librarian University Library Washburn University's University Libraries invites applications for Instructional Librarian to begin October 1, 2026. This is a 12-month, benefit eligible, full-time position. \n\nThe Instructional Librarian provides general and virtual information, research, and reference services, plans, teaches and assesses information literacy instruction in collaboration with the Associate Dean of University Libraries and other appropriate staff. In addition, based upon disciplinary interest, expertise, and Unit needs, the Librarian will support other library initiatives, including but not limited to: faculty and student research, digital projects, First and Second-Year Student Success Initiatives, collection development, scholarly communication, Open Access and Open Educational Resources, Artificial Intelligence, outreach, and assessment. Upward Bound Advisor University Library Washburn University is accepting applications for an Upward Bound Advisor. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) 435ff299 Last Name (required) 03e0dba5 Email (required) 4b82c63c Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you 1700 SW COLLEGE AVE TOPEKA, KANSAS 66621 785.670.1010 Memorial Union Mulvane Art Museum Disability Services Statements & Disclosures My Washburn Jobs Calendar Site Map Washburn University prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, age, national origin, ancestry, disability, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, genetic information, veteran status, or marital or parental status. The following person has been designated to handle inquiries regarding the non-discrimination policies: Michelle White-Godinet, Title IX Equal Opportunity Director, Washburn University, 1700 SW College Ave, Topeka, Kansas 66621, 785.670.1509, eodirector@washburn.edu . Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations, analyze our traffic and support our marketing efforts. By clicking “I Accept” or using the website you agree to our use of cookies. Please read our Web Privacy Statement for more information. If you prefer not to receive cookies, you may turn them off in your browser, or may set your browser to ask you before accepting a new cookie. I do not accept I accept Please choose the category/categories"
