    "https://careers.washburn.edu/jobs/graduate-assistant-ticketing-and-sales-topeka-kansas-united-states": {
      "title": "Graduate Assistant",
      "description": "Graduate Assistant - Ticketing and Sales - Topeka, Kansas, United States Home About Us Academics Admissions Student Life Athletics See all jobs Applicant Settings Kiosk mode Graduate Assistant - Ticketing and Sales Office of the Director of Athletics Apply Now Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Graduate Assistant - Ticketing and Sales Office of the Director of Athletics Student Add to favorites View favorites Position Title: Graduate Assistant - Ticketing and Sales Department: Athletics Advertised Pay: Stipend + Meal Plan Provided Campus Location: Washburn University Application Deadline: Application review will begin as applications are received and will continue until the position is filled. Applicants can be assured of full consideration if submitted by . Position Summary: This position offers a unique opportunity for a highly motivated and detail-oriented individual to gain hands-on experience in intercollegiate athletics. The selected candidate will play a vital role in supporting Washburn Athletics’ ticketing and sales efforts, enhancing customer service operations, and contributing to the development of corporate sponsorships. Reporting directly to the Director of Sales, the Graduate Assistant for Ticketing and Sales will assist with all aspects of ticket operations and revenue generation, helping to elevate the fan experience and drive engagement within the highly competitive Mid-America Intercollegiate Athletics Association (MIAA), the premier conference in NCAA Division II. This position is ideal for a graduate student pursuing a career in sports management, sales, or athletic administration. About Washburn University: Washburn University is a teaching-focused, student-centered, public institution located in the metropolitan setting of Topeka that has earned national recognition for its high-impact programs for first-generation students. Washburn has a student body of just over 7,000 students, a significant and growing number of whom are first-generation and Pell-Grant eligible. The University has created educational pathways for all students to be successful and achieve their educational goals. Washburn is dedicated to recruiting and retaining a dynamic faculty, staff, and student body and cultivating a robust learning and working environment and curriculum. We employ more than one thousand faculty and staff on our campuses throughout Topeka and strive to offer competitive wages, an excellent benefits program, and a supportive culture and a healthy work/life balance. Washburn seeks to create an environment that reflects our core values for creating positive IMPACT: inclusion, modernization, partnership, achievement, community and transformation. In 2024, Washburn was recognized as one of the best colleges in the nation to work for, according to Great Colleges to Work For® program. Essential Functions: -Assist with season ticket renewals and ticket sales for football, men’s basketball, and women’s basketball. -Support game day box office operations, including setup, ticket sales, and troubleshooting for all ticketed events, including football, volleyball, and basketball. -Manage camp registrations, including online setup, registration tracking, and customer communication. -Resolve ticketing issues and provide top-tier customer service through in-person, phone, and email support. -Assist with player passlist and Washburn Student All-Sport Pass registration. -Assist with the preparation of corporate sponsorship proposals, presentations, and other sales materials. -Research and develop sales leads for potential corporate sponsors and maintain sponsor tracking documents. -Help maintain and update the online ticket portal and generate sales and attendance reports. -Collaborate with staff to ensure a professional and efficient ticketing and sponsorship experience. Non-Essential Functions: -Perform other job-related duties as assigned or as appropriate. Required Qualifications: -Bachelor's degree. -Job contingent on admission and enrollment into the Washburn University Graduate School. -Availability to work evenings and weekends for athletic events as required. -Maintain a minimum cumulative and semester GPA of 2.5. -Ability to problem solve, manage multiple tasks, adhere to deadlines, and prioritize work. Preferred Qualifications: -Experience with Hometown Ticketing or similar ticketing platforms, Google Sheets, Canva, Microsoft 365, and Adobe Creative Suite products. -Background in sales, marketing, or sponsorships, particularly in a collegiate or sports setting. -Strong interpersonal, organizational, and written communication skills. Special Instructions to Applicants: Stipend Monthly Exempt Background Check Required Washburn University is committed to providing an environment for individuals to pursue educational and employment opportunities free from discrimination and/or harassment. The University prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, age, national origin, ancestry, disability, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, genetic information, veteran status, or marital or parental status. Washburn University is committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants for employment. If you are an applicant who needs a reasonable accommodation to participate in the application or interview process, please email benefits@washburn.edu or call 785-670-1538 at least five (5) business days in advance of the date you need the requested accommodation. Apply Now Want to hear about jobs like this one? First Name (required) 958ecc6e Last Name (required) 37030948 Email (required) dc843f48 Job Alert 8f06419e Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Office of the Director of Athletics Office of the Director of Athletics Categories Student Employee Student Employee Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Campus Safety Dispatcher (Part-time, Temporary) (Two Positions) University Police Washburn University is accepting applications to hire two Campus Safety Dispatchers. Technical Instructor (Associate Degree Nursing) WIT-Health Occupations Washburn University Institute of Technology seeks applications for a Technical Instructor for the Associate Degree Nursing program. There are currently two positions available for immediate hire. This is a 10-month, full-time position with benefits. This position is expected to work Monday-Friday 7:30 am – 4:00 pm. This position will also work varying clinical hours. Anthropology Special Project Lab Assistant Forensic Center Washburn University is accepting applications for an Anthropology Special Project Lab Assistant. Retail Specialist Memorial Union Washburn University is accepting applications for a Retail Specialist. Instructional Librarian University Library Washburn University's University Libraries invites applications for Instructional Librarian to begin October 1, 2026. This is a 12-month, benefit eligible, full-time position. \n\nThe Instructional Librarian provides general and virtual information, research, and reference services, plans, teaches and assesses information literacy instruction in collaboration with the Associate Dean of University Libraries and other appropriate staff. In addition, based upon disciplinary interest, expertise, and Unit needs, the Librarian will support other library initiatives, including but not limited to: faculty and student research, digital projects, First and Second-Year Student Success Initiatives, collection development, scholarly communication, Open Access and Open Educational Resources, Artificial Intelligence, outreach, and assessment. Upward Bound Advisor University Library Washburn University is accepting applications for an Upward Bound Advisor. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) 66d5c549 Last Name (required) 77eab483 Email (required) cbacf958 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you 1700 SW COLLEGE AVE TOPEKA, KANSAS 66621 785.670.1010 Memorial Union Mulvane Art Museum Disability Services Statements & Disclosures My Washburn Jobs Calendar Site Map Washburn University prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, age, national origin, ancestry, disability, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, genetic information, veteran status, or marital or parental status. The following person has been designated to handle inquiries regarding the non-discrimination policies: Michelle White-Godinet, Title IX Equal Opportunity Director, Washburn University, 1700 SW College Ave, Topeka, Kansas 66621, 785.670.1509, eodirector@washburn.edu . Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations, analyze our traffic and support our marketing efforts. By clicking “I Accept” or using the website you agree to our use of cookies. Please read our Web Privacy Statement for more information. If you prefer not to receive cookies, you may turn them off in your browser, or may set your browser to ask you before accepting a new cookie. I do not accept I accept Please choose the category/categories"
