    "https://careers.washburn.edu/jobs/instructional-librarian-topeka-kansas-united-states": {
      "title": "Instructional Librarian",
      "description": "Instructional Librarian - Topeka, Kansas, United States Home About Us Academics Admissions Student Life Athletics See all jobs Applicant Settings Kiosk mode Instructional Librarian University Library Apply Now Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Instructional Librarian University Library Faculty Lecturer Add to favorites View favorites Position Title: Instructional Librarian Department: University Library Campus Location: Washburn University Position Summary: Washburn University's University Libraries invites applications for Instructional Librarian to begin October 1, 2026. This is a 12-month, benefit eligible, full-time position. The Instructional Librarian provides general and virtual information, research, and reference services, plans, teaches and assesses information literacy instruction in collaboration with the Associate Dean of University Libraries and other appropriate staff. In addition, based upon disciplinary interest, expertise, and Unit needs, the Librarian will support other library initiatives, including but not limited to: faculty and student research, digital projects, First and Second-Year Student Success Initiatives, collection development, scholarly communication, Open Access and Open Educational Resources, Artificial Intelligence, outreach and assessment. Each selected candidate will have a demonstrated commitment to pursuing teaching excellence at Washburn University, including a dedication to developing inclusive teaching practices that engage all learners. About Washburn University: Washburn University is a teaching-focused, student-centered, public institution located in the metropolitan setting of Topeka that has earned national recognition for its high-impact programs for first-generation students. Washburn has a student body of just over 7,000 students, a significant and growing number of whom are first-generation and Pell-Grant eligible. The University has created educational pathways for all students to be successful and achieve their educational goals. Washburn is dedicated to recruiting and retaining a dynamic faculty, staff, and student body and cultivating a robust learning and working environment and curriculum. We employ more than one thousand faculty and staff on our campuses throughout Topeka and strive to offer competitive wages, an excellent benefits program, and a supportive culture and a healthy work/life balance. Washburn seeks to create an environment that reflects our core values for creating positive IMPACT: inclusion, modernization, partnership, achievement, community and transformation. In 2024, Washburn was recognized as one of the best colleges in the nation to work for, according to Great Colleges to Work For® program. Essential Functions: • Serve as liaison to academic departments. Locate and create digital content to support academic instruction. • Teach, integrate and assess Information Literacy programs across the curriculum. • Provide expert information and research services. • Explore, evaluate, and encourage the deployment of emergent technologies into library programs, information and instructional services. • Develop outreach strategies for students and faculty. • Participate in the building of physical and electronic collections that meet the needs of Washburn University. • Develop web and print-based materials. • Librarians are active members of internal library teams, Library and University Committees. • Perform additional job-related duties as assigned or as appropriate. Required Qualifications: • ALA-accredited master’s degree at the time of application or by the end of the semester of hire. • Experience providing reference or instruction services in archives, special collections, research libraries, museums, or cultural institutions. • Demonstrated understanding of issues and trends in reference and information literacy. • Proven effective interpersonal and communication skills. • Proven ability to work effectively independently and in teams. • Demonstrated experience providing accurate, proactive, and responsive information services. • Demonstrated dedication to developing inclusive teaching practices that engage all learners. • Official educational transcripts required at the time of hire. Physical Requirements: • Occasionally lift, carry, push, pull or otherwise move objects weighing less than 20 pounds Preferred Qualifications: • An additional master’s degree in any subject taught at Washburn University. • Demonstrated ability to work effectively independently or as part of a team. • Two years of experience providing reference or instruction services in archives, special collections or a research library, museum, or cultural institution. • Experience in a higher education library. Special Instructions to Applicants: Inquiries regarding this position may be directed to the Screening Committee Chair, Sean Stacey at sean.stacey@washburn.edu . Application Deadline: Application review will begin as applications are received and will continue until the position is filled. Applicants can be assured of full consideration if submitted by September 15, 2026. Background Check Required Washburn University is committed to providing an environment for individuals to pursue educational and employment opportunities free from discrimination and/or harassment. The University prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, age, national origin, ancestry, disability, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, genetic information, veteran status, or marital or parental status. Washburn University is committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants for employment. If you are an applicant who needs a reasonable accommodation to participate in the application or interview process, please email benefits@washburn.edu or call 785-670-1538 at least five (5) business days in advance of the date you need the requested accommodation. Apply Now Want to hear about jobs like this one? First Name (required) c636a87f Last Name (required) fa72dcc0 Email (required) bfb644f8 Job Alert ff9d967a Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments University Library University Library Categories Librarians Librarians Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Campus Safety Dispatcher (Part-time, Temporary) (Two Positions) University Police Washburn University is accepting applications to hire two Campus Safety Dispatchers. Technical Instructor (Associate Degree Nursing) WIT-Health Occupations Washburn University Institute of Technology seeks applications for a Technical Instructor for the Associate Degree Nursing program. There are currently two positions available for immediate hire. This is a 10-month, full-time position with benefits. This position is expected to work Monday-Friday 7:30 am – 4:00 pm. This position will also work varying clinical hours. Anthropology Special Project Lab Assistant Forensic Center Washburn University is accepting applications for an Anthropology Special Project Lab Assistant. Retail Specialist Memorial Union Washburn University is accepting applications for a Retail Specialist. Upward Bound Advisor University Library Washburn University is accepting applications for an Upward Bound Advisor. Police Officer (Two Positions) University Police The Washburn University Police Department is looking for interested individuals to join our team.  Washburn provides safety and security-related services on our main campus and affiliated campuses in Topeka, Kansas. Along with patrol duties, the Washburn Police work events on campus.  Washburn University provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees.  Start or continue your law enforcement career and apply today. Ready to Apply? First Name (required