me (17 items) 17 Staff Part-Time (1 items) 1 Staff Temporary (4 items) 4 Student (2 items) 2 Technical Instructor (4 items) 4 Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Police Officer (Two Positions) Topeka University Police Police and Public Safety Staff Full-time The Washburn University Police Department is looking for interested individuals to join our team.  Washburn provides safety and security-related services on our main campus and affiliated campuses in Topeka, Kansas. Along with patrol duties, the Washburn Police work events on campus.  Washburn University provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees.  Start or continue your law enforcement career and apply today. Read more Residential Community Coordinator Topeka Residential Living Residence Life, Housing Staff Full-time Washburn University is accepting applications for a Residential Community Coordinator position that is a full-time, live-in professional staff member responsible for creating a residential experience that supports student success, personal development, and community engagement. Read more Retail Specialist Topeka Memorial Union Retail, Sales, Merchandising Staff Full-time Washburn University is accepting applications for a Retail Specialist. Read more Senior Custodian Topeka Office of the Director of Athletics Custodians / Landscape Techs Staff Full-time Washburn University is accepting applications for a Senior Custodian. Read more Senior Maintenance Technician (Updated 7/7/2026) Topeka Facilities Services Facilities Maint/HVAC/Mgmt. Staff Full-time Washburn University is accepting applications for a Senior Maintenance Technician. Read more Technical Instructor (Associate Degree Nursing) Topeka WIT-Health Occupations Technical Careers Technical Instructor Washburn University Institute of Technology seeks applications for a Technical Instructor for the Associate Degree Nursing program. There are currently two positions available for immediate hire. This is a 10-month, full-time position with benefits. This position is expected to work Monday-Friday 7:30 am – 4:00 pm. This position will also work varying clinical hours. Read more Technical Instructor (Diesel Technology) Topeka WIT-Trades & Industry (Employment Prep) Technical Careers Technical Instructor Washburn Institute of Technology seeks applications for an Diesel Technology Technical Instructor to begin August 1, 2026, Monday through Friday, 7:30 a.m. to 4:30 p.m. This is a 10-month, benefit-eligible position. Position will be at the Washburn Tech Bruce & Teresa McPherson Campus in Topeka. Read more Technical Instructor (Medical Assistant) Topeka WIT-Health Occupations Technical Careers Technical Instructor Washburn University Institute of Technology invites applications for Technical Instructor in the Medical Assistant program. This is a 10-month, benefit eligible position with an August 1, 2026 start date. The program is in-person at the Washburn University Institute of Technology East Campus. Read more Technical Instructor (Practical Nursing-Evening Program) Topeka WIT-Health Occupations Technical Careers Technical Instructor Washburn Institute of Technology seeks applications for a Technical Instructor for the Licensed Practical Nursing Program. This role is an immediate opportunity. This is a 10-month, full-time position with benefits. This position will teach the evening program while also offering office hours. Monday through Thursday 1pm-9pm. The position will also work varying clinical hours, which may include an occasional weekend. Read more Upward Bound Advisor Topeka University Library Academic Advising, Student Success/Retention Staff Full-time Washburn University is accepting applications for an Upward Bound Advisor. Read more Displaying 31 - 40 of 40 in total ‹ 1 2 › 1700 SW COLLEGE AVE TOPEKA, KANSAS 66621 785.670.1010 Memorial Union Mulvane Art Museum Disability Services Statements & Disclosures My Washburn Jobs Calendar Site Map Washburn 